-- title:
--   Leading coefficient of the norm of g at Ogg's unit
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and set $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(jq)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $p$. Assume the Laurent series `modularUnitSeries p` $= \Delta(\mathfrak q)\,\Delta(\mathfrak q^{p})^{-1}$, formed from $\Delta = \mathfrak q \cdot (\text{Dedekind } \eta\text{-unit power series})$ and its substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{p}$, lies in $F$, and write $u \in F$ for the resulting element. Let $v \in F$ satisfy either $v = u$ or $v = p^{12} u^{-1}$. Let $g \in \mathbb{Z}[T]$ be monic with $\deg g \ge 1$ and $g(0) \neq 0$, and let $N \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ be such that, in $F$, the value of $N$ at `IgusaScheme.jFull p` (the element of $F$ given by the $\mathfrak q$-expansion of $j$) equals the image under the inclusion $\mathbb{Q}(j) \hookrightarrow F$, where $\mathbb{Q}(j)$ is the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $F$ generated by `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, of the norm $\mathrm{N}_{F/\mathbb{Q}(j)}(g(v))$. The conclusion is that there exist a unit $\varepsilon \in \mathbb{Z}^{\times}$ and a natural number $k$ with $\mathrm{lc}(N) = \varepsilon \, g(0)^{k}$. Only the existence of $k$ is asserted; no value for it is specified.
--
--   This is the leading-coefficient half of the analysis of norms, from the full modular function field of level $p$ down to $\mathbb{Q}(j)$, of polynomial expressions in Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(\mathfrak q)/\Delta(\mathfrak q^{p})$ and its Fricke transform $p^{12}/u$; its companion is the degree clause [`ModularCurve.natDegree_eq_mul_of_aeval_jFull_eq_norm_aeval_modularUnitSeries`](thm.html#ModularCurve.natDegree_eq_mul_of_aeval_jFull_eq_norm_aeval_modularUnitSeries). It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_int_poly_natDegree_aeval_jFull_eq_mul_aeval_modularUnitSeries`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_int_poly_natDegree_aeval_jFull_eq_mul_aeval_modularUnitSeries), which packages the existence of an integral polynomial realising such a norm together with its degree and leading-coefficient information.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_leadingCoeff_eq_mul_pow_of_aeval_jFull_eq_norm_aeval_modularUnitSeries.lean

